menu "Padel Court"

config PADEL_COURT_ID
    int "Court id"
    range 1 255
    default 1

config PADEL_COURT_WIFI_CHANNEL
    int "Wi-Fi channel"
    range 1 13
    default 1
    help
        ESP-NOW channel. Remotes must be configured to the same channel.

config PADEL_COURT_BUZZER_GPIO
    int "Buzzer GPIO"
    default 6
    help
        Sounder pin (spec section 15). GPIO6 is the free sensor-header pin on
        the 7B — the only one the RGB panel leaves alone. Verify against
        docs/HARDWARE_PINOUT.md on bring-up day.

config PADEL_COURT_BUZZER_PASSIVE
    bool "Buzzer is passive (driven with LEDC tones)"
    default y
    help
        A passive element has no oscillator of its own, so the firmware
        supplies the frequency and each cue gets its own pitch shape
        (ADR-0018). Turn this off for an active buzzer, which sounds at its
        own fixed pitch when the pin is driven high: the cues then differ only
        by rhythm, which is the fallback if the passive one is too quiet in
        the hall.

config PADEL_COURT_IDLE_DIM_MIN
    int "Idle minutes before the backlight dims"
    range 0 240
    default 10
    help
        Minutes without any input (touch, wired button, remote point or pair
        request) before the panel drops to the dim level below. 0 disables
        idle dimming entirely.

config PADEL_COURT_IDLE_DIM_PERCENT
    int "Idle dim backlight percent"
    range 0 100
    default 15
    help
        Backlight level held while idle. Never brighter than the organizer's
        own brightness setting. 0 disables idle dimming entirely.

config PADEL_COURT_IDLE_OFF_MIN
    int "Idle minutes before the backlight turns off"
    range 0 720
    default 30
    help
        Second stage: minutes of idle time before the backlight is cut
        completely (EXIO2 low). 0 keeps the panel at the dim level forever.
        The first touch afterwards only wakes the display; it never scores.

config PADEL_COURT_BUTTON_A_GPIO
    int "Wired backup button GPIO (Team A)"
    default 13
    help
        Arcade button, active low with internal pull-up. GPIO13 is a TF card
        pin; this firmware keeps its journal on internal-flash LittleFS and
        never touches the card, so 11/12/13 are free.

        Do not use GPIO16 here: it is RS485_RXD, wired to the *output* of the
        7B's onboard SP3485 transceiver, so a button pulling it low fights a
        driven pin.

config PADEL_COURT_BUTTON_B_GPIO
    int "Wired backup button GPIO (Team B)"
    default 15
    help
        GPIO15 is RS485_TXD, which feeds the transceiver's high-impedance
        input, so it is safe to repurpose while RS485 is unused.

endmenu
